### US-2 AC1 + AC2 + AC4 + RF-2 — card due by month
GET {{reports}}/card-due-by-month
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200
# {"rows":[
#   {"bucket":"Accrued","card":"PF Visa Liability",  "cycleYear":null,"cycleMonth":null,"amountMinorUnits":30000, "cardId":"01a05fdd-c367-7092-b5dc-b68516928b3c"},
#   {"bucket":"Future", "card":"01A05FDD-C367-…",     "cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":9,   "amountMinorUnits":30000, "cardId":"01a05fdd-c367-7092-b5dc-b68516928b3c"},
#   {"bucket":"Future", "card":"01A05FDD-C367-…",     "cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":10,  "amountMinorUnits":42000, "cardId":"01a05fdd-c367-7092-b5dc-b68516928b3c"},
#   {"bucket":"Accrued","card":"PF Master Liability", "cycleYear":null,"cycleMonth":null,"amountMinorUnits":100000,"cardId":"01a05fdd-c38f-73b9-b400-435490435e2c"},
#   {"bucket":"Future", "card":"01A05FDD-C38F-…",     "cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":9,   "amountMinorUnits":15000, "cardId":"01a05fdd-c38f-73b9-b400-435490435e2c"}]}
#
#   AC1 ✔ per-card "pay this month" = the Accrued bucket: PF Visa 30000, PF Master 100000 (one row per card).
#   AC2 ✔ Accrued holds only cuotas cerradas — Plan A inst1 (Aug). inst2/inst3 (Sep/Oct, cycle NOT closed)
#         are absent from Accrued; they only appear under Future.
#   AC4 ✔ Future bucket is a separate, per-cycle breakdown: PF Visa 2026-09 = 30000 (Plan A inst2),
#         2026-10 = 42000 (Plan A inst3 30000 + Plan C 12000); PF Master 2026-09 = 15000 (Plan D).
#   RF-2 fix ✔ every row — Accrued AND Future, both cards — now carries `cardId`. Accrued+Future for one
#         card share a case-safe key (Phase 7 could only tag buckets: Accrued keyed by account NAME,
#         Future by the UPPERCASE CardId GUID, no join possible). The `card` display column still differs
#         by bucket; `cardId` is the shared key.

### US-2 AC3 — same purchase date, different cutoff ⇒ different billing cycle
### PF Visa future-schedule (cutoff 15)
GET {{financing}}/cards/01a05fdd-c367-7092-b5dc-b68516928b3c/future-schedule
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200
# {"cardId":"01a05fdd-c367-…","rows":[
#   {"planId":"01a05fde-ae55-…","sequence":2,"cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":9, "amountMinorUnits":30000},
#   {"planId":"01a05fde-aeab-…","sequence":1,"cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":10,"amountMinorUnits":12000},   ← Plan C, purchase 2026-09-20
#   {"planId":"01a05fde-ae55-…","sequence":3,"cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":10,"amountMinorUnits":30000}]}

### PF Master future-schedule (cutoff 28)
GET {{financing}}/cards/01a05fdd-c38f-73b9-b400-435490435e2c/future-schedule
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200
# {"cardId":"01a05fdd-c38f-…","rows":[
#   {"planId":"01a05fde-aeb5-…","sequence":1,"cycleYear":2026,"cycleMonth":9,"amountMinorUnits":15000}]}   ← Plan D, purchase 2026-09-20
#
#   AC3 ✔ Plan C and Plan D were both purchased 2026-09-20. On PF Visa (cutoff 15) the 20th is AFTER the
#         cutoff ⇒ first cuota falls in the NEXT cycle → 2026-10. On PF Master (cutoff 28) the 20th is
#         ON/BEFORE the cutoff ⇒ first cuota falls in the CLOSING cycle → 2026-09. Same date, distinct
#         (CycleYear, CycleMonth) because the cycle is keyed off each card's corte, not the calendar.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# US-3 — Cargar un gasto en cuotas + reparto  (RF-3)
#   AC1 cargar con monto, tarjeta, cantidad de cuotas, fecha de compra
#   AC2 el ciclo de la 1ª cuota lo determina el sistema desde la fecha de compra + corte
#   AC3 opcionalmente, reparto entre N personas
#   AC4 el reparto suma exactamente al total (sin perder centavos)
#   AC5 después de cargarlo, la parte de cada persona es consultable
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### US-3 AC1 + AC3 — Plan B: PF Master, 100000 / 1, purchase 2026-07-10, split holder + Carol + Dave (1/1/1)
POST {{financing}}/payment-plans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 100000,
  "cardId": "01a05fdd-c38f-73b9-b400-435490435e2c",
  "installmentCount": 1,
  "purchaseDate": "2026-07-10",
  "split": [
    { "partyId": "01a05fde-29f6-79d3-9a7d-4db2a7c64abe", "weight": 1 },
    { "partyId": "01a05fde-2a18-72c7-a2e1-ca26066301c7", "weight": 1 }
  ]
}
# HTTP/2 201  {"paymentPlanId":"01a05fde-ae83-7d68-9171-841d98f211cf"}
#   AC1 ✔ body carries amount / card / installmentCount / purchaseDate.
#   AC3 ✔ optional N-way `split` accepted (holder implicit at weight index 0).
#
#   AC2 ✔ cutoff-driven cycle resolution, from the accrued installment rows:
#     sqlite3 personalfinance.db "SELECT pp.Id, i.CycleYear, i.CycleMonth FROM financing_installments i
#       JOIN financing_payment_plans pp ON pp.Id=i.PaymentPlanId;"
#       Plan B  2026 | 7    purchase 2026-07-10 ≤ Master cutoff 28  → ciclo que cierra (julio)
#       Plan C  2026 | 10   purchase 2026-09-20 >  Visa   cutoff 15  → ciclo siguiente
#       Plan D  2026 | 9    purchase 2026-09-20 ≤  Master cutoff 28  → ciclo que cierra (septiembre)

### US-3 AC4 — the split-aware accrual sums EXACTLY to the total
# After the Outbox drains (~2 s) OnPaymentPlanCreated records the split intent (AccruedReceivable = 0,
# D11 — not owed at plan creation) and links the receivable accounts. AccrueInstallments then posts the
# closed July cycle, tagged InstallmentReferenceId + SplitReferenceId:
#   sqlite3 personalfinance.db "SELECT a.Name, e.Direction, e.AmountMinorUnits FROM ledger_entries e
#     JOIN ledger_accounts a ON a.Id=e.AccountId
#     JOIN ledger_transactions t ON t.Id=e.TransactionId WHERE t.SplitReferenceId IS NOT NULL;"
#       PF Master Purchases  | Debit  | 33334      ← holder bucket takes the odd cent
#       PF Carol Receivable  | Debit  | 33333
#       PF Dave Receivable   | Debit  | 33333
#       PF Master Liability  | Credit | 100000
#   Σ debits = 33334 + 33333 + 33333 = 100000 = Σ credits.  PhantomPennyAllocator: Σ(parts) == total,
#   odd minor unit to the holder — no dropped, no duplicated centavo.
#   sqlite3 personalfinance.db "SELECT TotalMinorUnits, HolderShareMinorUnits, AccruedReceivableMinorUnits
#     FROM parties_expense_splits WHERE Source='CardPlan';"   →   100000 | 33334 | 66666

### US-3 AC5 — each participant's share is queryable after creation
GET {{parties}}/01a05fde-29f6-79d3-9a7d-4db2a7c64abe/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  {"partyId":"01a05fde-29f6-…","name":"PF Carol","balanceMinorUnits":33333}

GET {{parties}}/01a05fde-2a18-72c7-a2e1-ca26066301c7/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  {"partyId":"01a05fde-2a18-…","name":"PF Dave","balanceMinorUnits":33333}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# US-4 — Pagar el resumen de una tarjeta  (RF-4)
#   AC1 ver, antes de pagar, el detalle de qué cuotas componen el total
#   AC2 al confirmar el pago, deja de contar como deuda pendiente
#   AC3 distinguir un mes ya pagado de uno pendiente en el historial
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### US-4 AC1 — closest "before paying" view (see KNOWN GAP note below)
GET {{ledger}}/accounts/01a05fdd-c38f-7300-b0c3-1aa0abe67fc4/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  {"accountId":"01a05fdd-c38f-7300-…","balanceMinorUnits":100000,"currencyCode":"ARS","formatted":"1000.00 ARS"}
#   = the accrued PF Master Liability, i.e. the statement total about to be paid. The Accrued bucket of
#   /reports/card-due-by-month carries the same 100000. Neither breaks that figure into its component
#   installments-per-statement → see KNOWN FASE-1 GAP at the end of this block.

### US-4 — pay the PF Master July statement (AmountDue 100000)
POST {{financing}}/statements/01a05fdf-2e57-7130-b778-bcfded8f845d/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bankAccountId": "01a05fdd-c302-7f01-a653-ae8af14bdff1", "paidOnUtc": "2026-09-02T02:30:00Z" }

# HTTP/2 201  {"statementId":"01a05fdf-2e57-7130-b778-bcfded8f845d"}
#   pay txn legs:  Dr PF Master Liability 100000 / Cr PF Checking 100000   (no carried credit yet)

### US-4 AC2 — after paying, PF Master accrued liability is back to 0
GET {{ledger}}/accounts/01a05fdd-c38f-7300-b0c3-1aa0abe67fc4/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  {"accountId":"01a05fdd-c38f-7300-…","balanceMinorUnits":0,"currencyCode":"ARS","formatted":"0.00 ARS"}
#   (and /reports/card-due-by-month PF Master Accrued row now reads amountMinorUnits 0)

# US-4 AC3 — paid vs pending is distinguishable in stored state:
#   sqlite3 personalfinance.db "SELECT c.Name, s.CycleYear||'-'||s.CycleMonth, s.AmountDueMinorUnits,
#     COALESCE(s.PaidOnUtc,'(pendiente)') FROM financing_monthly_statements s
#     JOIN financing_credit_cards c ON c.Id=s.CardId;"
#       PF Visa   | 2026-8 | 30000  | (pendiente)
#       PF Master | 2026-7 | 100000 | 2026-09-02 02:30:00+00:00     ← IsPaid = PaidOnUtc is not null

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# US-6 — Corregir un error de carga  (RF-6)
#   AC1 revertir un gasto incluidas cuotas YA PAGADAS — el sistema no lo bloquea
#   AC2 reversión completa (futuras + pagadas), deja un movimiento de reversión (no un borrado)
#   AC3 si el gasto estaba repartido, la deuda del tercero se corrige en la misma acción
#   AC4 saldo propio y de la tarjeta reflejan la corrección completa
#   AC5 el historial muestra que fue revertido y cuándo
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### US-6 AC1 — reverse Plan B's accrual — whose installment was already PAID in US-4
POST {{ledger}}/transactions/01a05fdf-2e5a-7e6f-864c-f2c756c4e1e7/reversal

# HTTP/2 201
# {"reversalTransactionId":"01a05fe1-5cc1-7570-842c-6c642bee7d33",
#  "originalTransactionId":"01a05fdf-2e5a-7e6f-864c-f2c756c4e1e7","compensatingEntryPosted":true}
#   AC1 ✔ not blocked by the confirmed statement payment — HTTP 201, compensatingEntryPosted true.

# AC2 ✔ storno appended, original preserved, installment flagged (not deleted):
#   sqlite3 personalfinance.db "SELECT substr(Id,1,18), PostedOnUtc FROM ledger_transactions ORDER BY rowid;"
#     … 01A05FDF-2E5A-7E6F  2026-09-02 02:07:37…     ← original accrual, still present
#        01A05FE1-5CC1-7570  2026-09-02 02:09:59…     ← storno (exact mirror)
#        01A05FE1-5CCC-7F28  2026-09-02 02:09:59…     ← compensating (paid-installment leg)
#   storno legs  = Dr PF Master Liability 100000 / Cr PF Master Purchases 33334 / Cr PF Carol Rec 33333 / Cr PF Dave Rec 33333
#   installment  : sqlite3 … "SELECT Sequence, IsReversed FROM financing_installments
#                  WHERE PaymentPlanId='01A05FDE-AE83-7D68-9171-841D98F211CF';"  → 1 | 1

### US-6 AC3 — the split parties' debt is corrected by the same call
GET {{parties}}/01a05fde-29f6-79d3-9a7d-4db2a7c64abe/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  {"partyId":"01a05fde-29f6-…","name":"PF Carol","balanceMinorUnits":0}     (was 33333)

GET {{parties}}/01a05fde-2a18-72c7-a2e1-ca26066301c7/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  {"partyId":"01a05fde-2a18-…","name":"PF Dave","balanceMinorUnits":0}      (was 33333)
#
#   The storno's Cr Receivable legs moved the balances; Parties then only advances metadata (RNF-5, no
#   ledger post):  sqlite3 … "SELECT AccruedReceivableMinorUnits, ReversedReceivableMinorUnits
#     FROM parties_expense_splits WHERE Source='CardPlan';"   →   66666 | 66666

### US-6 AC4 — own + card balances reflect the full correction
GET {{ledger}}/accounts/01a05fdd-c38f-7300-b0c3-1aa0abe67fc4/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  balanceMinorUnits 0      PF Master Liability — net of accrual +100000, pay −100000, storno −100000, compensating +100000

GET {{ledger}}/accounts/01a05fdd-c396-7c48-ad1b-199bf2cf19fd/balance
Accept: application/json

# HTTP/2 200  balanceMinorUnits 100000     PF Master Credit — the compensating entry:
#   Dr PF Master Credit 100000 / Cr PF Master Liability 100000   ← NOT Cr Gasto:Categoría (D12 / DESIGN.md
#   doc-sync target — the storno already unwound the expense, so re-crediting Gasto would double count).
#   sqlite3 … "SELECT CarriedCreditBalanceMinorUnits FROM financing_credit_cards WHERE Name='PF Master';" → 100000
#   (carried credit nets the card's NEXT statement — the 2-leg / 3-leg forms are exercised in the Phase 10
#    D12 re-verification block above.)

# AC5 ✔ the reversal is in the history with its timestamp — storno row 01A05FE1-5CC1-7570,
#   PostedOnUtc 2026-09-02T02:09:59Z, append-only; the original 01A05FDF-2E5A row never disappears.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PRD §8 — success-metric check (checkable in principle, against this seed)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# "De utilidad real" (§8):
#   • "reemplaza el método anterior 4+ semanas" — needs real longitudinal use; not a checkpoint assertion.
#   • "el saldo de cada tarjeta coincide con el resumen del banco" — GET /accounts/{cardLiability}/balance
#     and the Accrued bucket (US-2 AC1/AC2) equal ONLY the cuotas cerradas = exactly what the bank will
#     bill; the temporal boundary (D11) is what makes this hold. Structurally checkable now.
#   • "el saldo con cada persona coincide con lo que reconoce" — GET /parties/{id}/balance + timeline
#     (US-3 AC5, US-6 AC3) is a live read of the Receivable account; reconciling against a real person
#     is out of scope for the checkpoint.
# "De aprendizaje" (§8): met by the suite — double-entry invariants (DoubleEntryMustBalance),
#   command/query separation, Outbox used only for PaymentPlanCreated (schedulers for clock work),
#   module isolation enforced by PersonalFinance.Architecture.Tests (RNF-9).

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# KNOWN FASE-1 GAP — US-4 AC1
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# "Puedo ver, antes de pagar, el detalle de qué cuotas componen el total a pagar de una tarjeta ese mes."
# There is no dedicated statement-detail endpoint. GET /reports/card-due-by-month (Accrued bucket) gives
# the per-card total; GET /financing/cards/{id}/future-schedule gives the un-accrued breakdown. Neither
# itemizes the installments rolled into one MonthlyStatement. Closing it = a small host route
# (GET /v1/financing/statements/{id} → its component installments) + one query; NOT added in this pass
# (no code green-light for Step 6). Recorded here as the one Fase-1 acceptance gap.

###
